/-! # Spreading finite algebras from the generic fibre

Source: blueprint, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra.md;
Stacks Project, Limits, Tag 01ZR (blueprint: lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra).

The pushout square in commutative ring sheaves expresses algebra scalar extension:
`O_generic ⊗_{g⁻¹ O_local} g⁻¹ B ≅ C`. Thus it records an algebra identification,
including multiplication and unit, rather than only an underlying module identification.
Product decompositions are limiting fans in the recorded category of algebra sheaves.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

set_option autoImplicit false

/-- Every finite coherent algebra on the generic fibre extends to a finite quasi-coherent
algebra after inverting one nonzero element of the base.
Source: blueprint, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra.md;
Stacks Project, Limits, Tag 01ZR (blueprint: lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra).
Proof:
1. The fraction field is the filtered colimit of the principal localizations at nonzero
   elements (lem-weil-pbc-localization-colimit-principal-localizations). Spec and base change
   give the corresponding affine-transition limit (lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition,
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs, lem-weil-pbc-scheme-over-limit).
2. Projectivity implies properness, separatedness and finite presentation over the
   Noetherian base (lem-pc-projective-proper, def-weil-proper-morphism,
   lem-pc-separated-quasi-separated, pqf-lem-lft-fp-locnoeth). Base changes are qcqs and of
   finite presentation (lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-morphism-permanence,
   lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-over-affine).
3. Coherence gives a finitely presented quasi-coherent underlying module
   (lem-weil-pbc-coherent-local-finite-presentation,
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine). Descend this module by
   lem-pc-fp-module-map-descent (1).
4. Tensor squares and cubes have finite presentations: tensor the finite generators and
   impose the relations from either factor. Use
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-tensor-product-affine-sections and
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine. Pullback preserves these presentations
   (lem-pc-tensor-pullback-finite-presentation), and commutes with tensor products
   (lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-tensor).
5. Descend multiplication, unit and, for a specified product, its finitely many coordinate
   idempotents, using lem-pc-fp-module-map-descent (2), at a common later stage.
6. The associativity, commutativity and two unit defects vanish generically. So do the
   idempotence, orthogonality and sum-to-one defects of the coordinate idempotents.
   Apply lem-pc-fp-zero-map-descent to this finite list and pass to a common later stage.
7. The descended multiplication and unit define a commutative algebra sheaf
   (def-weil-pbc-comm-algebra-sheaf). Its underlying finitely presented module is of finite
   type by lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine. The generic identification
   preserves multiplication and unit, giving the displayed scalar-extension pushout.
8. The images of the coordinate idempotents are quasi-coherent
   (lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-cokernel-image) and finite, generated by the images of
   a finite generating set. The maps x ↦ (eᵢx) and (xᵢ) ↦ ∑ xᵢ are inverse algebra maps.
   Their split projection identities persist under generic pullback, identifying the
   specified generic factors and projections.
9. For an empty product use the zero algebra and a = 1. The product of the finitely many
   nonzero denominators is nonzero in a domain. Empty schemes and zero factors are allowed. -/
theorem spread_finite_algebra
    (A K : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Field K] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    (T : Scheme.{u}) (f : T ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [IsProjective f]
    (C : (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K)))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
    (hC : RingedSpace.IsCoherent
      (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K)))).toRingedSpace
      C.toModule) :
    ∃ (a : A), a ≠ 0 ∧
      ∃ (φ : Localization.Away a →+* K)
        (g : pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K))) ⟶
          pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a)))))
        (B : (pullback f
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a))))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
        (θ : (TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).obj B.right ⟶
          C.right),
        φ.comp (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a)) = algebraMap A K ∧
        g ≫ pullback.fst f _ = pullback.fst f _ ∧
        g ≫ pullback.snd f _ = pullback.snd f _ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ) ∧
        B.toModule.IsQuasicoherent ∧ B.toModule.IsFiniteType ∧
        IsPushout
          ((TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).map B.hom)
          (Scheme.Modules.tensorPullbackRingMap g) θ C.hom := by
  sorry

/-- A specified finite product decomposition extends along with its finite coherent algebra,
with the same localization and with all generic projections identified.
Source: blueprint, sec-smooth-purity/sk-prop-sf-cbc/lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra.md;
Stacks Project, Limits, Tag 01ZR (blueprint: lem-fin-spread-finite-algebra).
Proof:
1. The fraction field is the filtered colimit of the principal localizations at nonzero
   elements (lem-weil-pbc-localization-colimit-principal-localizations). Spec and base change
   give the corresponding affine-transition limit (lem-weil-pbc-limit-affine-transition,
   lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs, lem-weil-pbc-scheme-over-limit).
2. Projectivity implies properness, separatedness and finite presentation over the
   Noetherian base (lem-pc-projective-proper, def-weil-proper-morphism,
   lem-pc-separated-quasi-separated, pqf-lem-lft-fp-locnoeth). Base changes are qcqs and of
   finite presentation (lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-morphism-permanence,
   lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-over-affine).
3. Coherence gives a finitely presented quasi-coherent underlying module
   (lem-weil-pbc-coherent-local-finite-presentation,
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine). Descend this module by
   lem-pc-fp-module-map-descent (1).
4. Tensor squares and cubes have finite presentations: tensor the finite generators and
   impose the relations from either factor. Use
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-tensor-product-affine-sections and
   lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine. Pullback preserves these presentations
   (lem-pc-tensor-pullback-finite-presentation), and commutes with tensor products
   (lem-weil-pbc-module-pullback-tensor).
5. Descend multiplication, unit and, for a specified product, its finitely many coordinate
   idempotents, using lem-pc-fp-module-map-descent (2), at a common later stage.
6. The associativity, commutativity and two unit defects vanish generically. So do the
   idempotence, orthogonality and sum-to-one defects of the coordinate idempotents.
   Apply lem-pc-fp-zero-map-descent to this finite list and pass to a common later stage.
7. The descended multiplication and unit define a commutative algebra sheaf
   (def-weil-pbc-comm-algebra-sheaf). Its underlying finitely presented module is of finite
   type by lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-finite-type-affine. The generic identification
   preserves multiplication and unit, giving the displayed scalar-extension pushout.
8. The images of the coordinate idempotents are quasi-coherent
   (lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-cokernel-image) and finite, generated by the images of
   a finite generating set. The maps x ↦ (eᵢx) and (xᵢ) ↦ ∑ xᵢ are inverse algebra maps.
   Their split projection identities persist under generic pullback, identifying the
   specified generic factors and projections.
9. For an empty product use the zero algebra and a = 1. The product of the finitely many
   nonzero denominators is nonzero in a domain. Empty schemes and zero factors are allowed. -/
theorem spread_finite_algebra_product
    (A K : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsDomain A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [Field K] [Algebra A K] [IsFractionRing A K]
    (T : Scheme.{u}) (f : T ⟶ Spec (.of A)) [IsProjective f]
    (C : (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K)))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
    (hC : RingedSpace.IsCoherent
      (pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K)))).toRingedSpace
      C.toModule)
    (I : Type u) [Finite I]
    (Cs : I → (pullback f
      (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K)))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
    (p : ∀ i : I, C ⟶ Cs i) (hp : IsLimit (Fan.mk C p)) :
    ∃ (a : A), a ≠ 0 ∧
      ∃ (φ : Localization.Away a →+* K)
        (g : pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A K))) ⟶
          pullback f (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a)))))
        (B : (pullback f
          (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a))))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
        (θ : (TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).obj B.right ⟶
          C.right),
        φ.comp (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a)) = algebraMap A K ∧
        g ≫ pullback.fst f _ = pullback.fst f _ ∧
        g ≫ pullback.snd f _ = pullback.snd f _ ≫ Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom φ) ∧
        B.toModule.IsQuasicoherent ∧ B.toModule.IsFiniteType ∧
        IsPushout
          ((TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).map B.hom)
          (Scheme.Modules.tensorPullbackRingMap g) θ C.hom ∧
        ∃ (Bs : I → (pullback f
            (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
              (algebraMap A (Localization.Away a))))).CommAlgebraSheaf)
          (q : ∀ i : I, B ⟶ Bs i)
          (θs : ∀ i : I,
            (TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).obj
              (Bs i).right ⟶ (Cs i).right),
          Nonempty (IsLimit (Fan.mk B q)) ∧
          ∀ i : I, (Bs i).toModule.IsQuasicoherent ∧ (Bs i).toModule.IsFiniteType ∧
            IsPushout
              ((TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).map (Bs i).hom)
              (Scheme.Modules.tensorPullbackRingMap g) (θs i) (Cs i).hom ∧
            (TopCat.Sheaf.inverseImageConstruction g.base CommRingCat.{u}).map (q i).right ≫
              θs i = θ ≫ (p i).right := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
